G\u001b[22mFor\u001b[48Gexample,\u001b[57G\"orders\u001b[65Gare\u001b[69Gfully\u001b[75Gloaded\u001b[82Gthrough\u001b[90G2026-10-25.\"\u001b[103GNori-Rel\u001b[112Gcan't\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bwork this out from the newes\u001b[36Grow,\u001b[41Gso you need to tell\u001b[61Gme.\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BIf\u001b[6Gyou'd like to try it before connecting your own data, I can \u001b[67Gun the wh\u001b[77Gle thing on Nori-Rel's built-\u001b[107Gn sample\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bdatabase (48\u001b[16Gc\u001b[18Gstomers and th\u001b[33Gir\u001b[36Gorder\u001b[42G)\u001b[44Gin a local Docker Postgres.\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GCrunched for 18s · done 5:58 PM\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mI want to know how much each user will spend in the next 30 days. The data is in PostgreSQL: the connection URL is in\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mthe DATABASE_URL environment variable, schema nori_rel_example, tables users and orders. The data is complete \u001b[39m        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mthrough 2026-03-02. Nori can run locally on this machine; nori-rel with the database and local extras is already \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255minstalled\u001b[13Gi\u001b[15G this Python.\u001b[39m                                                                                            \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;78;186;101m●\u001b[39m \u001b[1mSkill\u001b[22m(nori-rel:setup)\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mSuccessfully loaded skill\u001b[K\u001b[36;1H\u001b[34;3H\u001b[?25h"]
